rchived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310502,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA1MDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:import","name":"topic:import","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-05-07T10:30:01Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T14:50:54Z","closed_at":"2025-06-02T14:50:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.4\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Mint\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen reimporting fbx models with armatures, inherited scenes break. This seems to be tied to the animation player.\nThis happens even if the armature was not changed in Blender. My concrete example is a pistol with several bones. In the fbx import view the gun is shown correctly and when creating a new inherited scene it also shows it correctly. However when updating an existing scene, multiple bones of the gun object suddenly take on seemingly random rotations and positions. It should be noted that the skeleton itself is displayed correctly however the actual bone attachment nodes are displaced for some reason. The bones are even marked as having being changed from their original position, clicking reset will reset them, until you save at which point they will revert to their broken state as long as an active animation player is in the scene.\n\nThe animation player however does not even have tracks for all the parameters edited here, some bones aren't touched at all yet they are somehow altered by it.\nThis makes working exceedingly frustrating because every tiny change in blender will result in me having to either remake the entire scene or remake all animations.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n-Create a blender scene with multiple objects and bones\n-import as fbx\n-create inhereted scene and add animation player with bone animations\n-change something in the blender scene so it triggers a reimport\n-the inhereted scene is now broken\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106142/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned","pinned_comment":null}